      "message": "The change makes sense and it is the same fix you did already in https://github.com/eclipse-jdt/eclipse.jdt.ui/pull/3009, which had the same symptoms.\n\nHowever I am not completely sure the pre-conditions to use `setUseHashlookup(true)` (see [JavaDoc](https://github.com/eclipse-platform/eclipse.platform.ui/blob/16e4823269971757561ecc157e2df3368932c7a9/bundles/org.eclipse.jface/src/org/eclipse/jface/viewers/StructuredViewer.java#L1760-L1763)) are met:\n\n\u003e Note: enabling hash lookup requires from client code that elements managed by\n\u003e the viewer properly implement {@link #hashCode()} and {@link #equals(Object)}\n\u003e and that equal elements are not added to the same parent in the tree (each\n\u003e equal element should have a different parent chain).\n\nI see that the viewer ends up having `org.eclipse.egit.core.internal.rebase.RebaseInteractivePlan.PlanElement` inside, but that class only really implements `equals(...)`. `hashCode()` simply [delegates to `super`](https://github.com/eclipse-egit/egit/blob/6a6c76d62014d089edb83120bbb99c34cbc341fe/org.eclipse.egit.core/src/org/eclipse/egit/core/internal/rebase/RebaseInteractivePlan.java#L679)\n\n```java\n@Override\npublic int hashCode() {\n\treturn super.hashCode();\n}\n```\n\nWouldn\u0027t you have to provide a proper `hashCode` implementation for this fix to work as expected?",
